==Sundanese==

===Etymology===
Inherited from {{inh|su|osn|ma|t=marker of emphasis}}<ref>{{cite-journal|en|author1=Aditia Gunawan|author2=Evi Fuji Fauziyah|title=The particle ''ma'' in Old Sundanese|work=Wacana Journal of the Humanities of Indonesia|volume=22|issue=1|page=207-223|year=2021|pageurl=https://scholarhub.ui.ac.id/wacana/vol22/iss1/10/?lang=en}}</ref>

===Particle===
{{su-head|pcl}}

# {{non-gloss|unique marker of [[emphasis]], often untranslatable}}
#: {{ux|su|Abdi '''mah''' asalna ti Ciamis.|I ['''the topic, which we are talking about'''] am from Ciamis.}}
#: {{ux|su|Kamari '''mah''' abdi ka Singapur.|Yesterday, I went to Singapore.}}
#: {{ux|su|Poé ieu '''mah''' jigana bakal hujan.|It looks like it will rain today. (literally, "'''As for today''', it looks like it will rain".)}}

====Usage notes====
* Note that ''mah'' has no direct counterpart in both English and Indonesian. ''Mah'' is used as a focus marker to introduce a new information within a conversation or compare existing information.<ref>{{cite-journal|id|author=Deanty Rumandang Bulan|title=Sundanese emphasis particles téh, téa, and mah|work=Metamorfosis|volume=11|issue=1|page=10–14|year=2018|pageurl=https://doi.org/10.55222/metamorfosis.v11i1.24}}</ref> 

